% Generate `lib/playbook_generator.py`: OpenNolan's custom-playbook generator. When none
% of the built-in preset playbooks match a production brief, the agent builds a custom,
% schema-valid playbook dict (rather than forcing the brief through the closest preset)
% and saves it as YAML.
% Use `from __future__ import annotations`; import `json`, `yaml`, `jsonschema`,
% `pathlib.Path`, and `typing.Any/Optional`.

Module constants (all derived from the repo root = `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent`):
- `PLAYBOOK_SCHEMA_PATH` → `schemas/styles/playbook.schema.json`
- `STYLES_DIR` → `styles`
- `CUSTOM_STYLES_DIR` → `styles/custom`

`_load_playbook_schema()` loads and returns the schema JSON.

`load_existing_playbook(name) -> dict` loads `{name}.yaml` from `STYLES_DIR`, falling back to
`CUSTOM_STYLES_DIR`; raise `FileNotFoundError` if neither exists. Return `yaml.safe_load`.

`list_playbooks(*, packaged: Optional[bool] = None) -> list[str]` returns the sorted, de-duped
stems of every `*.yaml` under `STYLES_DIR` plus (if it exists) `CUSTOM_STYLES_DIR`. This must be
a SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH with `styles.playbook_loader`: import `PACKAGED_PLAYBOOKS` from it and
`lib.app_paths` locally (inside the function). When `packaged` is None, auto-detect via
`app_paths.is_packaged()`; when packaged, filter the names down to `PACKAGED_PLAYBOOKS` so the
agent cannot discover a hidden style through this enumerator. `packaged` overrides auto-detect
(for tests).

`generate_playbook(name, context, base_playbook: str | None = None) -> dict` builds a custom
playbook. Start from `load_existing_playbook(base_playbook)` if given, else
`_create_minimal_playbook(name, context)`. `context` is a dict of optional keys — `mood`, `tone`,
`pace`, `audience`, `colors`, `fonts`. Then override in place, applying each only if present:
- `identity.name` = `name` (always); `identity.mood` = `mood`; `identity.pace` = `pace`.
- `identity.category` = map `tone` → category: cinematic→`cinematic`, educational→`minimalist`,
  corporate→`motion-graphics`, playful→`motion-graphics`, raw→`cinematic`, else `custom`.
- `colors` (dict) overrides `visual_language.color_palette`: `primary`/`accent` are wrapped in a
  one-element list when given as a str (kept as-is if already a list); `background`/`text` set directly.
- `fonts` (dict) sets `typography.headings.font` and `typography.body.font`.
Return the mutated playbook.

`_create_minimal_playbook(name, context) -> dict` builds a minimal but complete, schema-valid
playbook from scratch. Default `mood`="professional", `tone`="corporate". Pick a palette by mood
bucket (each `primary`/`accent` is a list):

| mood bucket                    | background | text      | primary     | accent      |
|--------------------------------|------------|-----------|-------------|-------------|
| dark / cinematic / dramatic    | `#0F172A`  | `#F8FAFC` | `["#3B82F6"]` | `["#F59E0B"]` |
| warm / intimate / organic      | `#FFFBEB`  | `#1C1917` | `["#D97706"]` | `["#059669"]` |
| playful / energetic / bold     | `#FFFFFF`  | `#1F2937` | `["#7C3AED"]` | `["#EC4899"]` |
| else (professional/clean/etc.) | `#FFFFFF`  | `#1F2937` | `["#2563EB"]` | `["#F59E0B"]` |

Return this structure:
- `identity`: name, `category`="custom", mood, `pace`=`context.get("pace","moderate")`,
  `best_for`=`f"Custom playbook for {tone} {mood} content"`.
- `visual_language`: `color_palette` (primary, accent, background, text from the table),
  `composition`="balanced grid with breathing room", `texture`="clean digital".
- `typography`: headings `{font: "Inter", weight: 700}`, body `{font: "Inter", weight: 400}`.
- `motion`: `transitions`=["crossfade","cut"], `animation_style`="spring-based with moderate damping",
  `pacing_rules` = min_scene_hold 2.0, max_scene_hold 6.0, text_card_hold 3.5, stat_card_hold 4.0,
  transition_duration 0.4 (all `*_seconds`).
- `audio`: `voice_style`="clear, conversational, authoritative", `music_mood`=mood, `music_volume`=0.15.
- `asset_generation`: `image_prompt_prefix`=`f"{mood} {tone} style"`,
  `consistency_anchors`=[`f"{mood} color palette"`, `f"{tone} visual language"`].
- `quality_rules`: maintain color consistency across scenes; text legible on all backgrounds;
  transitions purposeful not decorative.
- `chart_palette`: `primary + accent + ["#10B981", "#EF4444", "#8B5CF6"]`.

`save_playbook(playbook, project_name: str | None = None) -> Path` validates the playbook against
the schema (`jsonschema.validate`), derives the filename from `project_name` or
`identity.name` lowercased with spaces and underscores replaced by hyphens, creates
`CUSTOM_STYLES_DIR`, writes `{filename}.yaml` (`yaml.dump`, `default_flow_style=False`,
`allow_unicode=True`), and returns the path.
